#: ../../../src/usage/precision.rst:4
msgid "Numerical Precision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/precision.rst:6
msgid ""
"By default, MLX may run ``float32`` matrix-multiplication family operations "
"(matmul, quantized matmul, grouped matmul, convolution and attention) at "
"reduced precision on hardware with dedicated matrix-multiplication units. "
"Inputs and outputs stay ``float32``, but results can differ from a full-"
"precision reference by several orders of magnitude more than ``float32`` "
"rounding alone would explain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/precision.rst:13
msgid ""
"To keep these operations in full ``float32``, set :envvar:`MLX_ENABLE_TF32` "
"to ``0`` when launching the process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/precision.rst:16
msgid "MLX_ENABLE_TF32=0 python my_script.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/precision.rst:20
msgid ""
"Which operations take the reduced-precision path, and how large the "
"difference is, depends on the backend and the hardware."
msgstr ""
